      "options": ["Tommy Vercetti", "100", "city", "Vice City"],
      "answer": 3
    },
    {
      "id": "q7",
      "text": "Why would we keep a date of birth in a tuple and not in a list?",
      "options": [
        "It should never change, and Python stops any code that tries to change it by mistake",
        "A tuple can hold more numbers than a list, and a date needs three",
        "A tuple keeps its numbers sorted, so the year always comes first",
        "A list can hold only text, and a date is made of numbers"
      ],
      "answer": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "q8",
      "text": "What does this print?",
      "code": "a, b = (10, 20)\nprint(b, a)",
      "options": ["10 20", "20", "(10, 20)", "20 10"],
      "answer": 3
    },
    {
      "id": "q9",
      "text": "What happens when this runs?",
